  "content": {
    "id": "v2-9f0a2-p19-practice-slot-8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Maya repays a loan by paying $\\$200$ in the first month, then $\\$20$ more each month than the month before. She has repaid $\\$3720$ in total. Find the number of months she has been repaying, and the amount of her last payment.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "12 months; $\\$420$.",
      "worked": "The monthly payments form an AP with $a=200$, $d=20$ and $S_n=3720$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\frac{n}{2}[2a+(n-1)d]\\\\3720&=\\frac{n}{2}[2(200)+(n-1)(20)]\\\\3720&=\\frac{n}{2}(380+20n)\\\\3720&=n(190+10n)\\\\n^2+19n-372&=0\\\\(n-12)(n+31)&=0\\\\n&=12\\quad(n>0).\\end{align*}$$\n\nShe has been repaying for 12 months. For the last payment:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=a+(n-1)d\\\\a_{12}&=200+11(20)\\\\a_{12}&=420.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHer last payment is $\\$420$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
